1.Get Product Stock
📌 Endpoint: GET /inventory/{productId}
📌 Description: Fetches available stock for a specific product.

📌 Response:
json
{
  "productId": "123",
  "availableStock": 50,
  "reservedStock": 10,
  "status": "IN_STOCK"
}

2.Bulk Stock Check
📌 Endpoint: POST /inventory/check-stock
📌 Description: Checks stock availability for multiple products in one request.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "products": [
    { "productId": "123", "quantity": 5 },
    { "productId": "456", "quantity": 10 }
  ]
}
📌 Response:
{
  "products": [
    { "productId": "123", "available": true },
    { "productId": "456", "available": false }
  ]
}

3. Update Inventory (After Purchase or Restock)
📌 Endpoint: PUT /inventory/update
📌 Description: Updates inventory after an order is placed or stock is replenished.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "productId": "123",
  "change": -5,  // -ve for order deduction, +ve for stock addition
  "reason": "ORDER_PLACED"
}

📌 Response:
json
{
  "productId": "123",
  "availableStock": 45,
  "status": "IN_STOCK"
}

4. Add New Product to Inventory
📌 Endpoint: POST /inventory/add
📌 Description: Adds a new product to the inventory system.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "productId": "789",
  "initialStock": 100,
  "reorderLevel": 10
}
📌 Response:

json
{
  "message": "Product added successfully",
  "productId": "789"
}

5. Reserve Stock for Order
📌 Endpoint: POST /inventory/reserve
📌 Description: Temporarily reserves stock for a customer’s order to avoid over-selling.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "orderId": "ORD123",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "123", "quantity": 2 },
    { "productId": "456", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}
📌 Response:
json
{
  "orderId": "ORD123",
  "status": "RESERVED"
}

6. Release Reserved Stock (On Order Cancellation)
📌 Endpoint: POST /inventory/release
📌 Description: Releases reserved stock when an order is canceled.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "orderId": "ORD123"
}

📌 Response:
json
{
  "message": "Stock released successfully",
  "orderId": "ORD123"
}

7.Deduct Stock (On Successful Order Payment)
📌 Endpoint: POST /inventory/deduct
📌 Description: Deducts stock permanently after an order is confirmed and paid for.

📌 Request:
json
{
  "orderId": "ORD123",
  "items": [
    { "productId": "123", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

📌 Response:
json
{
  "message": "Stock deducted successfully",
  "orderId": "ORD123"
}